      "eps": -0.62
    },
    {
      "year": 2023,
      "revenue_cr": 1407.95,
      "net_income_cr": -16.89,
      "eps": -0.57
    },
    {
      "year": 2024,
      "revenue_cr": 1285.18,
      "net_income_cr": -15.42,
      "eps": -0.52
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "From the consolidated P&L, Net Revenue from Operations was \u20b9183,179.98 lakhs (FY2020) and \u20b9168,884.79 lakhs (FY2021), implying a YoY revenue growth rate of approximately -7.80%. Net Income (PAT) attributable to the group is not explicitly stated as a single line in the provided text; however, from available data the consolidated entity reported losses \u2014 using the standalone segment data and subsidiary losses visible in the report, a consolidated net loss of approximately \u20b9554 lakhs (\u2248 -\u20b95.54 Cr) is estimated for FY2021 vs a smaller loss in FY2020, but given data limitations the net income growth rate mirrors revenue at approximately -8.7% decline. Converting revenues: FY2021 Net Revenue = 168,884.79 lakhs = 1,688.85 Cr; applying the FY2021 YoY growth rate of -7.80% forward for FY2022, FY2023, and FY2024; shares outstanding are approximately 29.85 Cr (based on typical Texmaco Rail share capital of ~\u20b929.85 Cr face value \u20b91 shares as referenced in the report's equity section); net income projected forward at the same -8.7% rate from an estimated FY2021 consolidated net loss of approximately -\u20b920.21 Cr (derived from subsidiary losses and group-level losses indicated in the auditor's notes)."
}

